##* {{RQ:Shakespeare Twelfth Night|act=III|scene=iv|page=267|column=2|passage=Madame, the young Gentleman of the Count ''Orſino''’s is return’d, I could hardly entreate him backe: he '''attends''' your Ladyſhips pleaſure.}}
##* {{RQ:Walton Compleat Angler|chapter=Epistle Dedicatory|page=13|passage=[I]f common Anglers ſhould '''attend''' you, and be eye-vvitneſſes of the ſucceſs, not of your fortune, but your skill, it vvould doubtleſs beget in them an emulation to be like you, and that emulation might beget an induſtrious diligence to be so: but I knovv it is not attainable by common capacities.}}
##* {{RQ:Johnson Rambler|issue=200|date=15 February 1752|page=119|passage=[He] told me, that he had promiſed to '''attend''' ſome ladies in the park, and, if I vvas going the ſame vvay, vvould take me in his chariot.}}
##* {{RQ:Prescott Philip 2|volume=I|chapter=Early Days of Philip|page=40|passage=In October, 1543, the Portuguese infanta quitted her father's place in Lisbon, and set out for Castile. She was '''attended''' by a numerous train of nobles, with the archbishop of Lisbon at their head.}}
